      "title": "Assistant Professor of Management",
      "description": "Providence College Job Opportunities | CAREER PAGE For full functionality of this page it is necessary to enable JavaScript. \n        Here are the instructions how to enable JavaScript in your web browser Assistant Professor of Management | CAREER PAGE page has loaded. Assistant Professor of Management | CAREER PAGE page has loaded. Click here or press any key to continue. Providence College Job Opportunities Menu Providence College Job Opportunities Sign In Don't have an account? Create one . Already have an account? Sign In . User profile dropdown menu for Username Applications Inbox Profile Account Sign Out After clicking on this link you will be logged out and the page will be reloaded. Applications Inbox Profile Go to Background Investigation Account Sign Out After clicking on this link you will be logged out and the page will be reloaded. Welcome! Thanks for creating an account. CAREER PAGE powered by NEOGOV ® Need this page in another language? You can translate this page using your browser's built-in translation feature. Tip: In Chrome or Edge, right-click anywhere on the page and select \"Translate to [Language].\" Assistant Professor of Management Print Apply ﻿ Assistant Professor of Management Salary See Position Description Location Providence College Job Type Ordinary Faculty Job Number PC00291 Division Academic Affairs Department Management Opening Date 09/08/2026 FLSA Exempt Bargaining Unit NU Description Benefits Conducted under the auspices of the Dominican Friars, Providence College is a Catholic, Dominican, liberal arts institution of higher education and a community committed to academic excellence in pursuit of the truth, growth in virtue, and service of God and neighbor. We seek candidates who can affirm and contribute to our mission. Providence College is also an equal opportunity employer and is committed to fostering a Beloved Community — an environment that reflects the rich diversity of the human family and is marked by justice, charity and the promotion of the common good and flourishing of all. We invite applications from qualified individuals who possess the experience, knowledge and commitment to develop the diverse learning environment envisioned as part of the Beloved Community. Women and minority candidates are strongly encouraged to apply. The College’s Non-Discrimination policy can be found Notice of Non-Discrimination (PDF document) Overview The Department of Management in the School of Business at Providence College is seeking a full-time, tenure-track faculty member at the rank of assistant professor commencing August 2027. Providence College is a nationally recognized institution known for excellence in undergraduate education, a strong liberal arts tradition, and a distinctive Catholic and Dominican mission. Its commitment to academic excellence and student success is reflected in consistent national recognition, including a #2 ranking among Regional Universities in the North in U.S. News & World Report ’s 2026 Best Colleges ranking, inclusion in Forbes ’ Top Colleges for 2026, and recognition as one of The Princeton Review ’s Best 391 Colleges for 2026. Housed in the Arthur F. and Patricia Ryan Center for Business Studies, the AACSB-accredited Providence College School of Business is a fast-growing and innovative academic community committed to excellence in teaching, scholarship, and student success. Nationally recognized for its undergraduate programs, the school is consistently ranked among the Top 50 best undergraduate business schools in the nation by Poets&Quants . The city of Providence, Rhode Island, offers an exceptional quality of life, combining the cultural and culinary amenities of a larger city with the accessibility and character of a close-knit community. Known for its acclaimed restaurant scene, vibrant arts and cultural community, historic architecture, and distinctive neighborhoods, Providence is also home to a rich higher education ecosystem, with eight colleges and universities contributing to the city’s intellectual and creative energy. The assistant professor will join the Department of Management , which consists of twelve (12) full-time faculty members and offers an undergraduate major in management, in addition to courses in management for the graduate business program. The assistant professor of management will contribute to the department’s teaching, research, and service missions. We welcome applicants representing a range of perspectives and areas of teaching and scholarship, with a particular interest in those whose work engages with teams, organizational behavior, and related micro-organizational research. A Ph.D. in management, organizational behavior, or a related field from an AACSB-accredited institution is required. ABDs with anticipated completion by the time of appointment will also be considered. Salary: $120,000-$135,000 Duties and Responsibilities Teaching: The assistant professor will be committed to high-quality teaching and student advising, and will teach six (6) courses during the academic year, across the fall and spring semesters, including undergraduate courses in management and courses at the graduate level as needed. There may also be opportunities to teach during the winter and summer semesters. Research: The assistant professor will be expected to conduct and publish high-quality research in their area of concentration. Maintenance of AACSB Scholarly Academic qualifications is required. Service: The assistant professor will be expected to engage in service activities for the department, school, and college, as well as ongoing practice-oriented activities consistent with AACSB qualification requirements as defined by the School of Business. Education and Experience A Ph.D. in management, organizational behavior, or a related field from an AACSB-accredited institution is required. ABDs with anticipated completion by the time of appointment will also be considered. Supplemental Information Please submit your application materials online . Review of applications will begin immediately and continue on a rolling basis until the position is filled. For full consideration, applications must be received by 11:59 p.m. EDT on September 25 , 2026 . Your application must include the following: Letter of interest Curriculum vitae Graduate/doctoral transcript(s) Teaching philosophy statement Teaching evaluations summary Research statement outlining current and future research agenda Contact information for three references (for letters of recommendation) Note: References will receive an automated email via NEOED with instructions and a link for uploading their letter of recommendation. Additional documentation may be required from candidates who will be subsequently invited for a campus visit. For questions regarding this position, please contact Search Committee Chair Dr. Matthew Eriksen at meriksen@providence.edu . NOTICE OF E-VERIFY PARTICIPATION Providence College participates in E-Verify to confirm the identity and employment authorization of individuals hired to work in the United States. Before submitting this application, please review the following documents: E-Verify Notice of Participation Right to Work By continuing with this application, you acknowledge that you have been informed of our participation in E-Verify and have had the opportunity to review these notices. Providence College offers a comprehensive range of valuable benefits to eligible employees, which are designed to: Promote the health and well-being of you and your family Provide financial security while you are working Build financial resources for retirement Help you balance personal and work responsibilities Provide educational opportunities for you and your family These benefits include but are not limited to health, dental, 403b retirement plan, flexible benefits plan, tuition benefits, employee assistance plan, college paid basic life insurance and long-term disability insurance, and paid time off. To learn more, please visit our Employee Benefits website by clicking the following link: https://human-resources.providence.edu/benefits/ Employer Providence College (RI) Address 1 Cunningham Square Providence, Rhode Island, 02918-0001 Phone (401) 865-2341 Website www.providence.edu Apply Please verify your email address Verify Email Providence College Job Opportunities Account Privacy Policy Terms Of Use Accessibility Statement Privacy Settings Copyright © 2026 Do not sell my personal information × For California residents, and to the extent NEOGOV sells your personal information as the term “sell” is defined under the California Consumer Privacy Act, you have the right to opt-out of the sale of your personal information by us to third parties at any time. This setting only applies to registered account holders that have opted-in for an Access Membership. If you wish to opt-out click follow these steps: Log into your Job Seeker Profile Click your name in the upper right-hand corner Select Account Settings Select the Preferences section Click the Edit button next to Access Membership Switch Toggle to off Click Save If you do not have a registered account this setting does not apply, however, you can review your right on our privacy policy . If you require further assistance, please email privacy@neogov.com × Accessibility Statement At Governmentjobs.com, Inc. d/b/a NEOGOV, we recognize the importance of making our products\n                    and services accessible to all individuals, including those with disabilities, and are continually\n                    working to improve the experience for all users. Commitment to Accessibility We are committed to following best practices, including the Web Content Accessibility Guidelines\n                    (WCAG) 2.1, Level AA, to the extent feasible, however, we do not warrant compliance with these\n                    standards or any other accessibility standards. We are continually enhancing our platforms to\n                    ensure greater accessibility, and we actively seek out opportunities to improve accessibility features. Ongoing Enhancements Accessibility is an ongoing effort, and we are regularly updating our technology, services, and content\n                    to address accessibility barriers. Our team is dedicated to identifying areas for improvement and\n                    making enhancements that allow all users, regardless of their abilities, to fully engage with our\n                    services. Feedback and Assistance We value feedback from our users. If you encounter any accessibility barriers while using our services\n                    or have suggestions on how we can improve, please reach out to us at accessibility@neogov.com.\n                    We will make every effort to resolve any concerns and consider alternative options where possible. Thank you for choosing NEOGOV. We remain dedicated to improving accessibility and creating an\n                    inclusive experience for all. CAREER PAGE Providence College Job Opportunities Menu Close Menu CAREER PAGE Providence College Job Opportunities Faculty Job Opportunities Job Categories Human Resources Catholic & Dominican Diversity & Inclusion at Providence College Notice of Non-Discrimination Annual Security and Fire Safety Report Other Disclosures Contact HR Help & Support Translate Support Job Application Job Details Applying as: | Support Close Close Cancel Clear SIGN Save We've updated our Privacy Policy and Terms of Use. Please, read and accept changes. Effective date: August 19, 2025 NEOGOV PRIVACY POLICY Contents 1. Introduction; Scope of this Policy. 2. Where We Are a Service Provider. 3. Personal Data We Collect About You and Why. 4. Cookies and Similar Tracking Technologies. 5. Online Analytics and Advertising. 6. Information We Disclose. 7. International Users. 8. Your Data Rights and Choices. 9. Notice to California Residents. 10. Your Rights and 