    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/providencecollege/jobs/5453936/associate-or-full-professor-of-health-sciences-associate-dean": {
      "title": "Associate or Full Professor of Health Sciences; Associate Dean",
      "description": "Providence College Job Opportunities | CAREER PAGE For full functionality of this page it is necessary to enable JavaScript. \n        Here are the instructions how to enable JavaScript in your web browser Associate or Full Professor of Health Sciences; Associate Dean  | CAREER PAGE page has loaded. Associate or Full Professor of Health Sciences; Associate Dean  | CAREER PAGE page has loaded. Click here or press any key to continue. Providence College Job Opportunities Menu Providence College Job Opportunities Sign In Don't have an account? Create one . Already have an account? Sign In . User profile dropdown menu for Username Applications Inbox Profile Account Sign Out After clicking on this link you will be logged out and the page will be reloaded. Applications Inbox Profile Go to Background Investigation Account Sign Out After clicking on this link you will be logged out and the page will be reloaded. Welcome! Thanks for creating an account. CAREER PAGE powered by NEOGOV ® Need this page in another language? You can translate this page using your browser's built-in translation feature. Tip: In Chrome or Edge, right-click anywhere on the page and select \"Translate to [Language].\" Associate or Full Professor of Health Sciences; Associate Dean Print Apply ﻿ Associate or Full Professor of Health Sciences; Associate Dean Salary See Position Description Location Providence College Job Type Ordinary Faculty Job Number PC00277 Division Academic Affairs Department School of Nursing and Health Sciences Opening Date 08/19/2026 Closing Date Continuous FLSA Exempt Bargaining Unit NU Description Benefits Conducted under the auspices of the Dominican Friars, Providence College is a Catholic, Dominican, liberal arts institution of higher education and a community committed to academic excellence in pursuit of the truth, growth in virtue, and service of God and neighbor. We seek candidates who can affirm and contribute to our mission. Providence College is also an equal opportunity employer and is committed to fostering a Beloved Community — an environment that reflects the rich diversity of the human family and is marked by justice, charity and the promotion of the common good and flourishing of all. We invite applications from qualified individuals who possess the experience, knowledge and commitment to develop the diverse learning environment envisioned as part of the Beloved Community. Women and minority candidates are strongly encouraged to apply. The College’s Non-Discrimination policy can be found Notice of Non-Discrimination (PDF document) Overview The School of Nursing and Health Sciences (SNHS) at Providence College (also referred to as “the College” or “PC”) invites applications for the position of Associate Dean of Health Sciences (also called “Associate Dean”) at the rank of Associate or Full Professor. The anticipated start date is August 2027, with the possibility of a January 2027 or spring 2027 start if applicable. The Associate Dean serves as a key member of the School’s leadership team and works closely with the Dean to advance the academic mission of the School of Nursing and Health Sciences. Reporting directly to the Dean, the Associate Dean provides leadership in academic affairs, including collaborating directly with the department chairs and program directors to ensure curricular and research excellence and operational effectiveness across the School. The Associate Dean has a particular focus and advises the Dean on matters related to existing and new academic programs, faculty development, student success, and long-term strategic priorities to advance the school’s growth and academic reputation of excellence in the health sciences. The successful candidate will hold a faculty appointment with primary teaching responsibilities in Health Sciences, while collaborating with faculty in Nursing and related majors focused on preparing students for careers in the health professions. Additional opportunities exist to develop new and innovative graduate programs in health sciences. As a tenured faculty member, the successful candidate will maintain an active program of scholarship consistent with their discipline, as well as mentor health sciences faculty to develop their scholarly goals and accomplishments. An additional exciting opportunity is for the Associate Dean to develop new health sciences and interdisciplinary research opportunities and collaborative ventures across the school and college to advance the scholarly reputation of Providence College as a leader in health sciences and health care innovation. The successful candidate will contribute meaningful professional and institutional service in accordance with the expectations of Providence College. Applicants with an earned doctorate in Health Sciences, Exercise Science, Human Physiology, or a closely related field are strongly encouraged to apply. This is an exciting and historic opportunity to join PC’s newly established School of Nursing and Health Sciences and shape an innovative, interdisciplinary curriculum for the next generation of students entering nursing and other health professions. The 153,000 sq. ft state-of-the-art Ben Mondor Center for Nursing and Health Sciences houses the School of Nursing and Health Sciences’ existing and future undergraduate and graduate programs. This one-of-a-kind facility opened in January 2025 and features the latest classroom design and technologies and showcase expansive clinical simulation and research facilities, including a human performance laboratory and environmental simulation chamber. The department features a purpose-built classroom for teaching microbiology for the health professions and courses on applied human anatomy and physiology using the latest virtual cadaver technologies. A student career education and advising center, along with conference and meeting space, is included as part of the inspiring resources intended for preparing the next generation of healthcare providers, researchers, and educators. As the student body at Providence College grows increasingly diverse, we have a strong preference for candidates who demonstrate a deep commitment to and proven ability in supporting the success of students from historically marginalized economic, social, and cultural groups. The salary for this position is between $125,000-$150,000. Duties and Responsibilities This is a tenure-track faculty position with an administrative appointment as Associate Dean. Essential administrative responsibilities associated with the Associate Dean role report directly to the Dean of the School of Nursing and Health Sciences. Faculty responsibilities, including teaching, scholarship, student advising, assessment, and departmental service, report to the Chair of the Department of Health Sciences. Primary teaching responsibilities will be at the undergraduate level and will include academic advising and service to the College. Education and Experience Candidates with an earned doctorate in Health Sciences, Exercise Science, Human Physiology, or a closely related field are encouraged to apply. A doctoral degree, demonstrated excellence in undergraduate and/or graduate teaching, and evidence of scholarly productivity are required for this faculty appointment. Supplemental Information Applicants should apply online at the College’s career site at: https://careers.providence.edu and submit a cover letter, curriculum vitae , teaching statement/philosophy and evidence of teaching effectiveness, undergraduate and graduate transcripts, and three letters of recommendation. For additional information, please contact Dr. Todd Olszewski, Health Sciences Department Chair, at tolszews@providence.edu . Review of applications will begin on October 1, 2026, and continue until the position is filled. NOTICE OF E-VERIFY PARTICIPATION Providence College participates in E-Verify to confirm the identity and employment authorization of individuals hired to work in the United States. Before submitting this application, please review the following documents: E-Verify Notice of Participation Right to Work By continuing with this application, you acknowledge that you have been informed of our participation in E-Verify and have had the opportunity to review these notices. Providence College offers a comprehensive range of valuable benefits to eligible employees, which are designed to: Promote the health and well-being of you and your family Provide financial security while you are working Build financial resources for retirement Help you balance personal and work responsibilities Provide educational opportunities for you and your family These benefits include but are not limited to health, dental, 403b retirement plan, flexible benefits plan, tuition benefits, employee assistance plan, college paid basic life insurance and long-term disability insurance, and paid time off. To learn more, please visit our Employee Benefits website by clicking the following link: https://human-resources.providence.edu/benefits/ Employer Providence College (RI) Address 1 Cunningham Square Providence, Rhode Island, 02918-0001 Phone (401) 865-2341 Website www.providence.edu Apply Please verify your email address Verify Email Providence College Job Opportunities Account Privacy Policy Terms Of Use Accessibility Statement Privacy Settings Copyright © 2026 Do not sell my personal information × For California residents, and to the extent NEOGOV sells your personal information as the term “sell” is defined under the California Consumer Privacy Act, you have the right to opt-out of the sale of your personal information by us to third parties at any time. This setting only applies to registered account holders that have opted-in for an Access Membership. If you wish to opt-out click follow these steps: Log into your Job Seeker Profile Click your name in the upper right-hand corner Select Account Settings Select the Preferences section Click the Edit button next to Access Membership Switch Toggle to off Click Save If you do not have a registered account this setting does not apply, however, you can review your right on our privacy policy . If you require further assistance, please email privacy@neogov.com × Accessibility Statement At Governmentjobs.com, Inc. d/b/a NEOGOV, we recognize the importance of making our products\n                    and services accessible to all individuals, including those with disabilities, and are continually\n                    working to improve the experience for all users. Commitment to Accessibility We are committed to following best practices, including the Web Content Accessibility Guidelines\n                    (WCAG) 2.1, Level AA, to the extent feasible, however, we do not warrant compliance with these\n                    standards or any other accessibility standards. We are continually enhancing our platforms to\n                    ensure greater accessibility, and we actively seek out opportunities to improve accessibility features. Ongoing Enhancements Accessibility is an ongoing effort, and we are regularly updating our technology, services, and content\n                    to address accessibility barriers. Our team is dedicated to identifying areas for improvement and\n                    making enhancements that allow all users, regardless of their abilities, to fully engage with our\n                    services. Feedback and Assistance We value feedback from our users. If you encounter any accessibility barriers while using our services\n                    or have suggestions on how we can improve, please reach out to us at accessibility@neogov.com.\n                    We will make every effort to resolve any concerns and consider alternative options where possible. Thank you for choosing NEOGOV. We remain dedicated to improving accessibility and creating an\n                    inclusive experience for all. CAREER PAGE Providence College Job Opportu