pt Bargaining Unit NU Description Benefits Conducted under the auspices of the Dominican Friars, Providence College is a Catholic, Dominican, liberal arts institution of higher education and a community committed to academic excellence in pursuit of the truth, growth in virtue, and service of God and neighbor. We seek candidates who can affirm and contribute to our mission. Providence College is also an equal opportunity employer and is committed to fostering a Beloved Community — an environment that reflects the rich diversity of the human family and is marked by justice, charity and the promotion of the common good and flourishing of all. We invite applications from qualified individuals who possess the experience, knowledge and commitment to develop the diverse learning environment envisioned as part of the Beloved Community. Women and minority candidates are strongly encouraged to apply. The College’s Non-Discrimination policy can be found Notice of Non-Discrimination (PDF document) (Download PDF reader) Overview Responsible for the daily operations of the arena, including but not limited to ice maintenance, cleaning, event set up/break down, equipment repairs and upkeep, and all other assigned duties to maintain the safe and effective operation of Schneider Arena.  Responsible for compliance with all NCAA and Providence College rules and regulations. Duties and Responsibilities Daily maintenance of the ice surface including operation of Zamboni and edger operation, and removal and installation of ice surface.  (40%) Clean locker rooms, hallways, lobby, bathrooms, and spectator seating.  (30%) Perform event set up and break down. (20%) Off-season work includes painting, general repairs, and heavy cleaning.   (10%) Education and Experience High school diploma At least two years of experience in an arena or sports venue with familiarity in ice equipment and operation or an equivalent combination of education and experience. Strong customer service skills required 